   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "widgets_values": [
    "# 10 · Put THIS face / jacket / bag / style into a new picture (Qwen-Image 2.1)\n**Use:** load 1–3 reference pictures → describe the new scene and name each reference as **image 1 / image 2 / image 3**\n(\"the woman from image 1 wearing the jacket from image 2 sits at the bar of the café from image 3\") → Run → `S6/ref_q21_*.png`.\n8 steps, cfg 1 (Turbo). \n\n| Knob | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| 2nd / 3rd reference | switch the extra Load Image nodes on (image 2, image 3) |\n| width / height | the new picture (1024×1280 = 4:5) |\n| scene | one sentence per reference; say what must stay (\"same face, hair and outfit\") |\n\n**Known habit:** it copies the reference's pose and camera (a frontal photo → a frontal face). Write the pose you want, or use\n`10_ref_klein` for natural new poses. Clean product-style references (plain background) work best.\n\n| Reference | Use | Why (series 6, 14 refs × 3 scenes) |\n|---|---|---|\n| object / product | **10_ref_product_krea** or 10_ref_qwen21 | emblem, buckle, stitching survive (DINOv2 bag 0.87 / 0.85) |\n| garment (print, embroidery) | **10_ref_qwen21** | koi embroidery + lemon print closest |\n| face / whole character | **10_ref_qwen21** | ArcFace 0.81–0.92 from ONE photo (our Maren LoRA: 0.55) — but it copies the photo's frontal pose |\n| new pose / new camera angle | **10_ref_klein** | re-stages naturally (sits, turns, walks); details a bit looser |\n| art style / film look | **10_ref_qwen21** | gouache, risograph, Cinestill look on new content |\n| place | 10_ref_qwen21 (same view) · 10_ref_klein (other viewpoint) | Qwen keeps the exact room, Klein can turn the camera |\n| palette / light only | **10_ref_style_krea** | Qwen and Qwen-Edit 2511 paste the reference picture as the background |\n| 2–3 references at once | **10_ref_qwen21**, toggles 2nd / 3rd | face + jacket + café all kept |"
   ]
  },
